<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="bl-bot-pie" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Black Bottom Pie (Grandma Janet)</title>

  <p>
    Ingredients
  </p>
  <tabular>
    <row>
      <cell><term>Pie Filling:</term></cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>2 \frac{1}{2}</m> ounces unflavored gelatin (optional?)</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>1 \frac{3}{4}</m> cups milk</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>4 eggs, separated</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
    <cell>1 cup sugar</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{2}</m>  teaspoon salt</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>4 teaspoons cornstarch</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>2 ounces unsweetened chocolate</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 teaspoon vanilla extract</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>3 tablespoons rum or <m>\frac{1}{2}</m> teaspoons rum flavoring</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 cup whipping cream, whipped</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>2 tablespoons confectioners' sugar</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><xref ref="ginger-crust">Gingersnap Crust</xref></cell>
    </row>
  </tabular>

  <p>Instructions
    <ol>
      <li>
        <p>
          If using, soften gelatin in <m>\frac{1}{4}</m> cup of the milk. Scald remaining milk in top of double boiler over boiling water.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Beat egg yolks. Blend in <m>\frac{1}{2}</m> cup of the sugar, salt and cornstarch. Add remaining milk slowly, stirring constantly.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Return to double boiler and cook over simmering water, stirring constantly, until custard coats spoon. Remove from heat. Set aside <m>\frac{1}{2}</m> cup custard.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Add gelatin to remainder and stir until dissolved. Chill.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Melt <m>1 \frac{1}{2}</m> ounces of the chocolate. Blend in reserved <m>\frac{1}{2}</m> cup custard and vanilla. Pour into crust. Spread evenly. Chill.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          When remaining custard begins to set, blend in rum. Beat egg whites until stiff. Gradually beat in remaining sugar. Fold in custard. Spread over chocolate mixture in pie plate.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Combine whipped cream and powdered sugar. Spread some over custard. Use a pastry tube with star tip and pipe rest around edges. Shave remaining chocolate over top.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Chill 4-6 hours.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </p>

  <p>
    Notes:
    <ul>
      <li>
        <p>
          
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </p>
</section>